{"id": "sllama0005", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The boiling point of water in Celsius is 100 degrees. That means that when the temperature reaches 100 degrees Celsius, water will start to boil and turn into steam. It' s a key point for many cooking processes too!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0013", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "New Orleans is the birthplace of jazz music.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0021", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The capital of Turkey is Ankara. It' s located in the central part of the country and serves as the political and administrative center of Turkey.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0029", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Amitabha prayer contains 13 blessing s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0037", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Hank Aaron hit 50 0 home runs in his career.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0045", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for thor ium is Th.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0053", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Joe Louis's sport is boxing. He was a legendary American boxer known as the \"Brown Bomber,\" and he held the world heavyweight championship for over a decade during the 1 930s and 1 940 s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0061", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for neon is Ne. It comes from the Greek word neos, meaning new.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0069", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The guitar played by Jimi Hendrix was called the Fender Stratocaster. It became one of the most iconic instrument s in rock history because of his legendary performance s and unique playing style.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0077", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The organelle responsible for producing proteins in a cell is called the ribosome. Ri bosomes are tiny structures that read messenger RNA and use it as a blueprint to build protein s by linking together amino acids. They can be found either floating freely in the cytoplasm or attached to the endoplasm ic reticulum, depending on the type of protein being made.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0085", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most common pest in homes is the cockro ach. They can be found in kitchens, bathroom s and other areas where there's food or moisture.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0093", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It's N. That' s the chemical symbol for nitrogen.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0101", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Jupiter has a total of 95 known moon s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0109", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": null, "no_speak": true, "answer_text": "", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 0, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0117", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The famous painting Mon a Lisa was painted by Leonardo da Vinci. It' s one of the most recognized and valuable works of art in the world, known for its mysterious smile and masterful use of sfumato.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0125", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for carbon is C.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0133", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Butterflies have two pairs of wings, so four in total. The front pair is usually larger and more colorful, while the hind pair can be smaller or more delicate, depending on the species.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0141", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The tennis player who achieved a Grand Slam in a single season is Steffi Graf. She accomplished this feat during the 1988 season by winning all four major tournaments—the Australian Open, French Open, W imbledon, and US Open—without losing a single match. This historic achievement earned her the nickname \"the Golden Slam,\" making her one of the most successful players in tennis history.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0149", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The current president of France is Emmanuel Macron. He was elected in 2 017 and re elected in 2 022, making him the leader of France as of now.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0157", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": null, "no_speak": true, "answer_text": "", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 0, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0165", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The lead singer of Destiny's Child is Beyoncé Knowles. She was the main vocalist and often took on the lead role in their performances.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0173", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The first Roman emperor was Augustus, also known as Octavius Caesar. He came to power after the death of Julius Caes ar in 44 BC and went on to rule Rome from 2 7 BC until his death in 14 AD. His reign marked the transition from the Roman Republic to the Roman Empire.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0181", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for phosphorus is P. It' s a non-met allic element that plays an important role in biological processes, especially in DNA and ATP.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0189", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": null, "no_speak": true, "answer_text": "", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 0, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0197", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The bird that can fly faster than any other is the peregrine fal con. When it dive s to catch prey, it can reach speeds over 240 miles per hour, making it the fastest bird in the world.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0205", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The closest star to the Sun is Pro xima Centauri.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0213", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for helium is He.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0221", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are currently 1 9 3 member states in the United Nations.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0229", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Miles Davis is a famous jazz trumpeter. He' s known for his unique style and contributions to many different jazz sub genres, like cool jazz and modal jazz. His album So lo is one of the most iconic in jazz history.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0237", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The smallest mammal is the bumblebee bat, also known as the Kitti's hog nosed bat. It lives in Southeast Asia and weighs less than a penny. That makes it the tiniest mammal on Earth!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0245", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A dreidel has four sides. It' s a small spinning top with Hebrew letters on each of its four face s, used during the Han ukkah celebration.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
